@host = http://localhost:5000
@agentId = 8
@driverId = 7
@bookingId = 2

### Step 1: Submit a Draft Booking
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingID": {{bookingId}}
}

### Step 2: Agent fetches pending bookings
GET {{host}}/api/bookings/agent/{{agentId}}/pending
Accept: application/json

### Step 3: Agent accepts the booking (Generates Stage 1 & Stage 2 Delivery Tasks in DB)
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/accept
Accept: application/json

### Step 4: Driver fetches the unassigned task pool (Stage 1 pickup task should be visible)
GET {{host}}/api/deliverytasks/pool
Accept: application/json

### Step 5: Driver claims Stage 1 task
POST {{host}}/api/deliverytasks/1/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deliveryStaffID": {{driverId}}
}

### Step 6: Driver completes Stage 1 task (Pickup complete, booking status transitions to InProgress)
POST {{host}}/api/deliverytasks/1/complete
Accept: application/json

### Step 7: Agent marks the booking as Ready (Laundry processing done, waiting for Stage 2 driver)
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/ready
Accept: application/json

### Step 8: Driver fetches the task pool again (Stage 2 delivery task is now visible because Stage 1 is Completed and Booking is Ready)
GET {{host}}/api/deliverytasks/pool
Accept: application/json

### Step 9: Driver claims Stage 2 task
POST {{host}}/api/deliverytasks/2/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deliveryStaffID": {{driverId}}
}

### Step 10: Driver completes Stage 2 task (Delivery complete, parent booking status transitions to Completed)
POST {{host}}/api/deliverytasks/2/complete
Accept: application/json
